 "note": [
  "Scripture source: the Indian Revised Version (IRV Hindi, CC BY-SA 4.0), fetched as USX from the ebible mirror (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx), all 66 books. Every mined span was sliced from that text by script, never typed. Moody quotes the KJV almost entirely without chapter and verse; the translators located each quotation by search, and no citations were added.",
  "Title agreement: the book is प्रबल प्रार्थना, the phrase the Hindi school-of-prayer plan card (data/plan_translations/hi.json, job #695) already uses for Moody's part, so the card and the book agree. That curated plan stays dormant in Hindi: lord-teach-us-to-pray-2 has no Hindi edition yet.",
  "Derived by measurement: a row is mined only when the translator reported the quotation verbatim AND the measurement confirms it (a 6+ character quoted segment of that block, or an 8+ character phrase in the chapter, is a byte substring of the cited IRV verse). adapted/self rows and 5 unconfirmed verbatim claims (Dan 9:23 ch01, Matt 3:8 ch04, Heb 4:16 x2 ch09, Prov 12:1 ch11) are self_rendered. Unquoted echoes are not recorded. 125 mined, 42 self_rendered.",
  "KJV/IRV divergences an editor should see (IRV kept inside the quotation marks; Moody's point carried in his own sentences): Luke 11:1 'Lord, teach us to pray' (ch01, self — the IRV has it only inside a longer clause, and misspells सीखा); Matt 14:30 + 'or I perish' (ch01, blended with Matt 8:25); Job 40:4 उँगली दाँत तले for 'hand upon mouth' (ch02, loses the tie to the chapter's definition of adoration); Isa 1:13 'even the solemn meeting' (ch03); Ps 139:23 चिन्ताओं for 'thoughts' (ch03); Isa 61:8 'robbery for burnt offering' and Ps 35:13 'returned into mine own bosom' (ch04, self); Heb 13:15, 2 Chr 20:21, Isa 63:8 (ch05); Acts 2:1 has no 'with one accord' (ch07 — carried in narration); Jude 3 'common salvation' (ch07, self); John 14:14 IRV adds मुझसे (ch08); John 16:24 + Luke 11:9 conflated as Moody quotes them (ch09); Acts 9:6 'Lord, what wilt thou have me to do?' is not in the IRV — Paul's retelling Acts 22:10 हे प्रभु, मैं क्या करूँ? is used (ch11); Acts 26:28 'almost persuaded' (ch11, self); Phil 4:13 has no 'Christ' (ch11). Luke 23:34 keeps the IRV's own 'कर रहें हैं' byte-exact (ch06).",
  "Conventions: curly quotation marks mirror the English per chapter; the reader addressed as तुम, God in prayer as तू; Christ in the singular; prayer vocabulary आराधना, अंगीकार, भरपाई, धन्यवाद, क्षमा, एकता, विश्वास, विनती, अधीनता pinned as the chapter titles; numbers in the running text written as words where the English has none as digits; hymn stanzas keep every line break and signature.",
  "ENGLISH SOURCE items NOT repaired (the Hindi renders the evident sense): ch02 'Jairus worshiped Him' is the unnamed ruler of Matt 9:18 (Moody's conflation, kept); ch03 'Mathew Henry', 'O, God'; ch04 Isa 58:8 'thy reward' (a misprint of the KJV 'rereward'); ch08 the nobleman 'fell on his knees' and Luke 7:9 'to the Jews' (Moody's details, kept); ch09 b5 'cannot be expected answer'; ch11 b41 speaks of smoking then only of drink."
 ],
